# chip — the next-level hier vehicle (2026-07-30): three instances each of
# big2 (flow/big_data_test/big2/tc3b_flat_x5.buda, 44 blocks / 2840 nets, as a
# flat-script cell) and mix2 (flow/rnr/mix2.bdb.sql, 100 leaf blocks / 1270
# nets, imported as a BDB cell — build_hier_demo's one-level flatten), SA-placed
# with 25% bloat channels, plus 100 random cross-instance top buses:
# 6 instances, 432 leaf blocks, 13320 nets.  Rebuild recipe (deterministic
# iteration budget) in flow/chip/ReadMe.md.
#
# TOP-DOWN variant: the plain hier pipeline, healed with negotiate_congestion
# ONLY.  ripup_reroute is not affordable at this scale — it ran >10 minutes
# without converging here against a 135s base flow — and refine_selection is an
# end-of-flow WL polish that wants a converged endpoint.  For the healerless
# fast-iteration mode drop the negotiate_congestion line and the
# `set_planner_param healersAhead 1` above it; see flow/chip/ReadMe.md.
source chip_tracks.buda
open_bdb chip.bdb.sql
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
set_max_bundle_bits auto
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
set_planner_param healersAhead 1
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
negotiate_congestion
report_wl
check_design
exit
